questions:
This study investigates how germline genetic variants, pharmacogenomic profiles, behavioral factors, and environmental exposures influence drug response and outcomes in rare and genetic diseases. 
Using the All of Us multi-omic and longitudinal data, we aim to:
1. Characterize germline genetic variants and related clinical phenotypes;
2. Assess interactions between pharmacogenomic markers and treatment outcomes such as enzyme replacement or chaperone therapy;
3. Evaluate behavioral and environmental factors that may affect disease progression and treatment outcomes.
This research will advance precision medicine for rare diseases by integrating genetic and non-genetic determinants of therapeutic response, supporting more personalized and effective care for individuals with rare and genetic disease.

